<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66472" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεσο-πᾰγής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεσσο-</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παγῆναι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fixed up
				to the middle</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεσσοπαγὲς δ᾽ ἄρ᾽
				ἔθηκε κατ᾽ ὄχθης μείλινον ἔγχος</span> drove it in
				<i>up to the middle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.172
			</span></i>:—<i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> preferred the v.l.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεσσοπαλές</span></b> , <i>quivering
				up to the middle</i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>); but it is doubtful whether -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλές</span> could mean <i>quivering</i>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεσσοπαγής</span> is found in late Poets, as
				<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				1.233
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
